function smart_sort_array($set, $order) {
    usort($set, function($a, $b) use ($order) {
        return $order === 'asc' ? $a['age'] - $b['age'] : $b['age'] - $a['age'];
    });
    return $set;
}
```

The `usort()` function in PHP is used to perform user-defined sorting. Inside the lambda function passed to `usort()`, we compare the values of the `age` keys of both arrays (`$a` and `$b`) based on the value of the `$order` parameter. If `$order` is 'asc', we return the difference between the ages of the two arrays. If `$order` is 'desc', we reverse the order of the comparison. This will sort the elements of the `$set` array based on their `age` keys according to the provided `$order`.

